'''Timothy Morrison''' (born April 3, 1963) is an American former professional [[American football|football]] [[cornerback]] who played in the [[National Football League]] (NFL) for the [[Washington Redskins]]. He played [[college football]] at the [[University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill]].<ref>[https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/M/MorrTi20.htm Tim Morrison Stats]. ''Pro-Football-Reference''. Retrieved February 22, 2022.</ref> His nephew [[Antwoine Sanders]] was also a football player.<ref name="bio">{{cite web | url=http://www.utahutes.com/sports/m-footbl/mtt/sanders_antwoine00.html | title=Antwoine Sanders | publisher=utahutes.com | accessdate=24 December 2024 | archive-date=June 4, 2016 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160604052211/http://www.utahutes.com/sports/m-footbl/mtt/sanders_antwoine00.html | url-status=dead }}</ref>
